<title>UK: Canadian official sees wheatcrop down at 25 mln ts.</title>
<headline>Canadian official sees wheatcrop down at 25 mln ts.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Canada's 1997-98 wheat crop will fall by around 19 percent to about 25 million tonnes, Lorne Hehn, the chief commissioner of the Canadian Wheat Board, told reporters in London on Thursday/  </p>
<p>The total includes some 4.5 to 5.0 million tonnes of durum wheat, Hehn said.</p>
<p>He cited &quot;some drought in the south of the grain belt&quot;,  as well as reduced area as reasons for the decline.</p>
<p>Hehn was attending the annual International Grains Council meeting in London.</p>
